        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7aa85203-53f4-5970-92e3-1980177e2fa4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lloyd Kaufman, Michael Herz, Giuseppe Andrews, Jay T. Wright\n- Companies: Troma Entertainment\n- Works: The Toxic Avenger, Tromeo and Juliet, All the Love You Cannes!, Trailer Town\n- Topics: Film careers, film distribution, narrative tension\n\nFacts:\n- Stanley Lloyd Kaufman, Jr. was born on December 30, 1945, and he is an American film director, producer, screenwriter, and actor.\n- Lloyd Kaufman and producer Michael Herz co-founded the film studio Troma Entertainment.\n- Lloyd Kaufman directed many Troma Entertainment feature films, including The Toxic Avenger and Tromeo and Juliet.\n- In many of Jay T. Wright's films, tension acts as a competing motive and is sometimes in direct conflict with narrative.\n- All the Love You Cannes! is a 2002 documentary film directed by Lloyd Kaufman.\n- Trailer Town is a 2003 low-budget film shot on digital video, written and directed by Giuseppe Andrews, and distributed by Troma Entertainment.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
